      "answer": "SQL injection authentication bypass works. By sending `{\"username\": \"admin' --\", \"password\": \"anything\"}`, the server authenticated me as admin with full privileges.\n\n**Response:**\n```json\n{\n  \"authenticated\": true,\n  \"user\": \"admin\",\n  \"role\": \"admin\",\n  \"secret\": \"zauth-5d20-bypass\"\n}\n```\n\nThe bypass works because the `username` field is concatenated directly into an SQL query without parameterization. The `--` comment sequence truncates the remaining query, so the password check is never enforced \u2014 only the username condition matters, and `\"admin' --\"` matches the admin user.\n\nI can now log in as admin without knowing the password, gaining access to the `secret` value `zauth-5d20-bypass` and any other admin-only functionality.",
